  "description": "Our versatile Steilacoom platform offers excellent handling in a lightweight and durable package. Best-in-class mud clearance, standard rack and fender mounts, now with disc brakes ONLY…new pics on the way!Production sizes 49, 52, 55, 58 and 61 cm.\nTitanium\nProduction Frame\nOur versatile Steilacoom platform offers excellent handling in a lightweight and durable package. Best-in-class mud clearance, standard rack and fender mounts, now with disc brakes.\nSteilacoom: (STEEL-a-koom) Chinook name of a Native American village once located on Chambers Bay near present day Tacoma, Washington.\nSPECS:\nAggressively shaped and oversize tube set for maximum performance and light weight.\nS-bend seat and chain stays provide clearance for the thickest mud and the widest tires.\nRocker drop outs and chain stay Belt Break are standard for single speed and Gates Belt drives, ISO or Flat mounts mounts.\nSlightly sloping top tube. Smaller, lighter and stiffer main triangle and more stand-over height while still being easy to shoulder for run ups.\nT47 BB shell and 44mm headtube for increased rigidity and options for bearing sets in both cranks and forks.\nForward facing seat slot and seatpost binder reinforce the clamp area and keeps water out of your bottom bracket.\nSize specific geometry.",
